      "body": "Per audit mandate, please provide a risk assessment for the recurrence of Incident SA-2024-15 (unauthorized access to citizen records via the 'BenefitsView' portal) within the next 12 months.\n\n**Incident Summary:** On July 15, 2024, a contractor's credential was used to perform bulk queries outside of authorized scope, extracting 150 records. Root cause: Over-provisioned role ('Data Analyst - Full') assigned incorrectly via an automated onboarding script.\n\n**Remediation Status (as of Sept 5):**\n- The specific contractor's access was revoked July 16. (Completed)\n- The faulty onboarding script was deactivated July 20. (Completed)\n- A project to implement Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) review for all contractor accounts is in the 'planning phase,' expected completion date H2 2025.\n\n**Industry Benchmark Data (from State CIO Council Report 2023):**\n- Base rate for 'significant unauthorized data access incidents' in state-level benefits administration systems: 1.2 events per agency per 5-year period.*\n- *Footnote 12: 'Significant' defined as >100 records accessed without business need. This definition matches our incident.\n- *Footnote 13: Rate is for events where primary root cause is misconfigured access controls.\n\n**Remediation Effect Estimate (from CISO's office):**\n- Fixing the specific script reduces likelihood of an identical incident by 100%.\n- Implementing the full RBAC review (when done) would reduce the likelihood of *any* similar misconfiguration incident by 85%. Until RBAC is live, the reduction for similar-but-not-identical incidents is 0%."
    },
    {
      "sender": "CISO",
      "time": "2024-09-05 14:22",
      "body": "Noted. For the assessment period (next 12 months), the RBAC review is not complete. Therefore, for a *similar* incident (different vector, same root cause class), the applicable remediation reduction is 0%. The base rate provided is per 5 years. We have addressed the exact script flaw, so the identical incident cannot recur."
    }
  ]
}

